# Git conventions and workflow

## Language

All git-related text must be in **English** (see also `english-language.mdc`): commits, branches, PR titles/descriptions, issues, and review comments.

## Commit messages

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org):

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

### Types

| Type | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting, no logic change |
| `refactor` | Neither feat nor fix |
| `perf` | Performance |
| `test` | Tests |
| `chore` | Build, tooling, deps |
| `ci` | CI config and scripts |

### Scope and description

- Scope: affected component (e.g. `feat(auth): add login with Google`).
- Imperative, present tense; lowercase first word; no trailing period.

### Repo tooling

- Split multi-topic work: invoke project skill `.cursor/skills/commit-split/` (`/commit_split`); respects `.gitignore`.
- Do not commit unless the user asks; do not push unless asked.

## Branch names

```
<type>/<short-description>
<type>/<ticket>-<short-description>   # when tracked in issue tracker
```

Examples: `feat/add-google-auth`, `fix/PROJ-456-handle-null-responses`.

## Workflow

1. **Protected branches:** `main` (or `master`) — no direct commits; merge via PR.
2. **Feature work:** branch from `main`, commit with conventional messages, rebase on `origin/main` before push.
3. **Pull requests:** target `main`; clear title/body; tests green; resolve conflicts; prefer squash merge when appropriate.
4. **Releases:** `release/vX.Y.Z` from `main`, merge via PR, then tag on `main` (e.g. `v1.0.0`).

## Examples

```bash
# Good
feat(auth): implement JWT authentication
fix(api): handle null response from server
docs(mvp): align cheap-stocks spec with architecture

# Bad
Fixed stuff
WIP
Quick fix
```

## MCP Git

When using MCP Git tools (not the default shell workflow in this repo):

- Check branch before commit; never commit on `main`/`master` without a feature branch.
- Review diffs before staging and committing.
- Normalize `repo_path` per **`mcp-git-path-encoding.mdc`** (forward slashes, absolute path, no URL encoding).
